Public Hearings/Rules & Reg’s
14. PUBLIC HEARING regarding amendments to the amended 2019
Laramie County Land Use Regulations.
24 - 078
2019 Laramie County Land Use Regulations
Amendments
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said the board provided notice of intent to amend the 2019
amended Laramie County Land Use Regulations (LCLUR) on Jan 2, 2024.
Arnold stated legal notice was published in the Wyoming Tribune Eagle on Jan 12,
2024, and an open house was held with feedback from the public regarding the
proposed changes on Jan 24, 2024. He said the Planning Commission held a public
hearing on the proposed changes Feb 8, 2024, and voted 4-0 to recommend
adopting the changes. Arnold noted the amendments are to resolve inconsistencies
and clarify vague language until the larger project to overhaul the LCLUR is completed
and presented to the board later this year.
Chairman Lovett opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Hearing no PUBLIC
COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Holmes, seconded by
Commissioner Thompson, to adopt the changes to the Laramie County
Land Use Regulations as noted in the attached staff report from Jan 2,
2024. The motion carried by the following vote:
Lovett, Malm, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
