### Page 5 of 6

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
February 20, 2024
Land Use:Variances/Board App./Plats
15. PUBLIC HEARING regarding board approval for ATR Landscaping,
located at Tract 6, Antelope Hills, 1st Filing, Laramie County, WY.
24 - 080
ATR Landscaping
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Suzy Troncin, on behalf of ATR Landscaping, submitted
an application to allow a landscaping business on property located at Tract 6,
Antelope Hills, 1st Filing, Laramie County, WY. He said the parcel is situated in the
A-1 - Agricultural and Rural Residential Zone District, and under Land Use
Regulations § 4-2-101, landscaping businesses require board approval in the A-1
zone district.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval with the
adoption of findings of fact a and b with one condition: A site plan with pertinent
building permits must be approved by Laramie County Planning & Development
before business commences.
Chairman Lovett opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Steven Harrington, Al
Harris, Chris Marlow, and Robin Vinzant, residents, did not express concerns about
the landscaping business but requested the county maintain Highland Rd due to the
deteriorating condition of the road and anticipated increased use.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the hearing.
Commissioner Malm expressed disappointment that the applicant was not present at
the meeting. He asked Molly Bennett, Public Works, about maintenance of
surrounding roads in the area. It was noted that the majority of roads in the area are
taken care of by the county. Bennett said Highland Rd is publicly dedicated but not
maintained. She requested time to do additional research and present her findings at
a later meeting. Commissioner Malm said the board would look into the road
maintenance issue but could not make any promises.
Arnold recommended the board place an additional condition for the site plan to be
returned to the board for review. He said the applicant must bring the road up to
county standards for the site plan process.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Malm, seconded by Commissioner
Thompson, to grant board approval with condition one as outlined in the
staff report and adopt findings of fact a and b of the staff report;
additionally, the applicant must bring the site plan back before the
governing body for approval. The motion carried by the following vote:
Lovett, Malm, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
The meeting adjourned at 4:04 pm.
Page 5 of 6
